e\nHistory\nMathematics and Statistics\nPhilosophy\nPhysics and Astronomy\nPolitical Science\nPsychology\nSociology\nTheatre and Film\nWorld Languages and Cultures\nSchools\nSchool of Art\nSchool of Cultural and Critical Studies\nSchool of Earth, Environment and Society\nSchool of Media and Communication\nStudents\nCurrent students\nDegree audit\nEducation Abroad\nFind your advisor\nGPA calculator\nMajors and checksheets\nScholarships\nTransfer credit evaluation\nUndergraduate Student Handbook\nFuture students\nAdvanced Placement\nMajors and checksheets\nWelcome Future Falcons\nLearning communities\nAll learning communities\nArts Village\nFinding Your Voice in Social Justice\nGlobal Village\nFaculty\nResources\nChairs and Directors Handbook\nJob openings\nCollege forms\nSoftware site license agreements\nArts and Sciences committees\nArts and Sciences Council\nCouncil of Chairs and Directors\nCurriculum, Teaching and Learning committee\nDistinguished Teaching Award committee\nPromotion and tenure review committee\nUniversity committees\nFaculty Senate representatives\nUndergraduate Council representatives\nUniversity-level review committee\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nInfo for...\nFuture students\nCurrent students\nFirelands campus\nParents/families\nFaculty/Staff\nAlumni\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nToggle high contrast\nApplying for Admission/Assistantship\nBGSU\nCollege of Arts and Sciences\nAbout our Math and Statistics Programs\nGraduate Programs\nApplying for Admission/Assistantship\nBGSU uses an all-electronic application system. Apply online. There, you will:\nupload electronic scans of transcripts from all colleges or universities attended (Note: after admission, you will need to send BGSU official paper transcripts from each institution where you earned a degree.)\nupload a statement of purpose\nlist three faculty or professionals who can upload a letter of recommendation in support of your application; the application system will contact them by email.\nif you choose to submit a GRE score, send it to BGSU using Institution Code: 1069.\ninternational students, list your TOEFL or IELTS scores. Have TOEFL or IELTS scores sent to BGSU (Note: students from certain countries or with a master's degree from the US are exempt, see this link).\npay a non-refundable application fee ($45 domestic, $75 international)\nindicate your interest in being considered for a teaching assistantship (Note: Assistantship decisions are made in February/March, and offers go out shortly after that.)\nindicate the program you wish to pursue:\nMaster of Arts in Mathematics, choose Mathematics - MA\nMA specialization in Statistics, choose Mathematics: Statistics - MA\nMA specialization in Applied Mathematics / Scientific Computation, choose Mathematics: Applied Mathematics / Scientific Computation - MA\nPhD in Mathematics, choose Mathematics - PhD\nPhD in Statistics, choose Statistics - PhD\nIf you are an international student and are admitted to BGSU, please follow the instructions on the International Student Services webpage in order to obtain your non-immigrant documents. Please do this promptly after admission to avoid any delays.\nMore information on the application process at BGSU\nGraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs in Mathematics and Statistics at BGSU\nPh.D. Programs\nMaster Programs\nCertificate in Mathematics for Professionals and Educators\nApplying for Admission/Assistantship\nPeer Mentoring Program\nSummer Head Start Program\nFinancial Support\nRequest More Information\nStudent Testimonials\nGraduate Programs in Applied Mathematics\nFrequently Asked Questions\nStudent Code of Conduct\nDepartment of Mathematics & Statistics\nDr. Junfeng Shang, Chair\n419-372-2636\nmath-stat@bgsu.edu\n450 Mitchell B. McLeod Hall\nBowling Green State University\nBowling Green, OH 43403\nUpdated: 06/29/2026 02:30PM\nBowling Green State University\nBowling Green, Ohio 43403-0001\n419-372-2531\nAccessibility including events\nAcademics\nA-Z Links\nCampus Directory\nCons